  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: B</p>\n<p>B: The displacement <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"s\"></span> for an object starting from rest with constant acceleration <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\"></span> is given by the equation <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"s = \\frac{1}{2}at^2\"></span>. This indicates a direct proportionality between <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"s\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t^2\"></span>, which is represented by a straight line passing through the origin.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A metal block is released from rest at the top of a smooth inclined plane. Which of the following graphs best represents the variation of the displacement <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"s\"></span> of the block from its starting position with the square of the time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t^2\"></span> elapsed?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_04\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 4\" src=\"asset:fig_04\"/></figure></p></li></ol>"
  },
